<title>GERMANY: Anzag to raise 96 dividend by 28 pct.</title>
<headline>Anzag to raise 96 dividend by 28 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>German drugs wholesaler Andreae-Noris Zahn AG (Anzag) said it plans to raise its dividend 28.5 percent for the business year ended August 31, 1996.</p>
<p>The group plans to pay an 18 mark dividend per share, nominally valued at 50 marks, compared with the previous payout of 14 marks.</p>
<p>More details will be disclosed at the group's news conference on January 30.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
